  "body": "## What changed\n- Split work-offset frame classification (`OffsetFrame::Yaw` vs tilted `OffsetFrame::Rotated`) in `crates/app/src/posting_wcs_rotation.rs`.\n- Carry pure Z-axis WCS rotation into milling toolpath generation via `WcsYaw` (`crates/app/src/operation/wcs_yaw.rs`, `generate.rs`, `job.rs`, `stamp.rs`, `drill_prior.rs`), `SlotBound::rotated_xy` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/slot_room.rs`), and `Dexel::rotated_z_conservative` (`crates/sim/src/stock_sim/dexel.rs`).\n- Rotate generated `Toolpath`, `Region`, and located errors back to Setup table frame `S` before simulation, verification, workholding checks, fixture linking, and machine travel limit checks.\n- Add `WcsRotationOutput` (`Bake` default, `Control` opt-in) across schema, project DTOs, posting, MCP `set_post_options`, setup sheet, and the Post Options UI (`crates/app/src/schema.rs`, `posting.rs`, `project/*`, `mcp/post_options_tools.rs`, `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`, `crates/ui/src/egui_app/post_options.rs`).\n- Add `crates/post/src/post/wcs_rotate.rs` and `controller.coordinate_rotation` / `wcsRotation` capability checks across `.mch` and five `.cps` posts (`fanuc`, `haas`, `mazak`, `doosan-dnm` emit `G68`/`G69`; `sinumerik` emits `ROT RPL=`/`ROT`).\n- Refuse probing, turning, EDM, 5-axis/3+2 moves, and XZ/YZ arcs under a Z-rotated WCS, and guard `Align WCS (3-2-1)` against tilted faces on `Kind::Mill` (`crates/app/src/setup_wcs_tilt.rs`, `crates/ui/src/vertex_pick.rs`, `geo_page.rs`).\n\n## Cause\nMilling strategy generators and rest-prior grids ran directly in setup table coordinates `S`, ignoring any Z rotation on the setup WCS. Posting also rejected every rotated offset unconditionally regardless of whether only Z yaw was present.\n\n## Tests\n- Pins (`crates/post/tests/wcs_rotate.rs`): `bake_keeps_setup_table_coordinates_without_g68`, `control_mode_emits_g68_or_rot_only_when_machine_and_post_declare_it`, `mch_parser_reads_optional_controller_coordinate_rotation`, `probing_or_non_xy_arc_under_rotated_wcs_refuses_by_name`, `five_axis_abc_move_in_rotated_wcs_refuses_by_name`.\n- Pins (`crates/app/tests/wcs_rotation_carry.rs`): `face_passes_and_bake_post_follow_90_deg_z_rotated_wcs`, `face_passes_and_bake_post_align_to_30_deg_yaw`, `changing_wcs_yaw_marks_generated_op_stale`, `machine_travel_limits_check_physical_table_coordinates_under_rotated_wcs`, `setup_sheet_states_z_rotation_without_refusing_while_tilt_still_refuses`.\n- Pins (`crates/app/tests/wcs_rotation_control.rs`): `control_rotation_fanuc_emits_g68_g69_and_preserves_viewer_map`, `control_rotation_sinumerik_and_capability_refusals`, `rotated_wcs_carries_pocket_slot_circular_and_drill_ops`, `rotated_wcs_carries_pocket3d_rest_prior_grid`.\n- Pins (`crates/app/tests/rotated_wcs.rs`, `crates/ui/src/egui_app/wcs_align_guard_tests.rs`, plus `mcp_post_options.rs` and `setup_post_options.rs`): `the_post_stream_carries_z_offset_rotation`, `a_tilted_work_offset_is_refused_by_name`, `the_setup_sheet_states_the_offset_rotation`, `align_wcs_321_refuses_tilted_side_face_on_mill_and_names_part_alignment`, `align_wcs_321_allows_top_face_with_z_yaw_on_mill`.\n- Mutation 1: reverted `operation/{job.rs, generate.rs}` -> `face_passes_and_bake_post_follow_90_deg_z_rotated_wcs` failed -> restored, passed.\n- Mutation 2: reverted `operation/stamp.rs` -> `changing_wcs_yaw_marks_generated_op_stale` failed -> restored, passed.\n- Mutation 3: reverted `post/engine.rs` -> 4/5 tests in `crates/post/tests/wcs_rotate.rs` failed -> restored, passed.\n- Mutation 4: mutated `OffsetFrame::Yaw` in `posting_wcs_rotation.rs` to refuse -> `face_passes_and_bake_post_follow_90_deg_z_rotated_wcs` failed -> restored, passed.\n- Mutation 5: reverted `ui/{vertex_pick.rs, egui_app/geo_page.rs}` -> `align_wcs_321_refuses_tilted_side_face_on_mill_and_names_part_alignment` failed -> restored, passed.\n- Gate & clippy: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed (`post`, `sim`, `motion`, `app`, `ui`; 0 failed); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n\n## UI review evidence (#2136)\n\nThese are 1600 × 1000 GPU-rendered egui shell captures from the same `ShellUi::seeded()` document and camera (`Block` 60 × 60 × 30 mm, `Contour1`). Images live only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch (`78e0bb35eb710981386ef24748b635bbc9d32f5d`).\n\n| View | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Post Options (`WCS rotation`) | ![Before: Post Options without WCS rotation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/78e0bb35eb710981386ef24748b635bbc9d32f5d/2136/post-options-before.png) | ![After: Post Options with WCS rotation picker](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/78e0bb35eb710981386ef24748b635bbc9d32f5d/2136/post-options-after.png) |\n| Operation Geometry (`Align WCS (3-2-1)`) | ![Before: Align WCS enabled for tilted side face](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/78e0bb35eb710981386ef24748b635bbc9d32f5d/2136/align-321-before.png) | ![After: Align WCS disabled with Part alignment refusal tooltip](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/78e0bb35eb710981386ef24748b635bbc9d32f5d/2136/align-321-after.png) |\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone (`git diff --stat -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty).\n\n## Not exercised\n- Full non-quick `cargo xtask gate` outside `gate quick --base upstream/main`.\n- Execution of posted `G68` / `ROT RPL=` code on physical CNC controls.\n- Other `.cps` scripts beyond `fanuc`, `haas`, `mazak`, `doosan-dnm`, and `sinumerik` in `Control` mode (they remain allowed in `Bake` and refused in `Control`).\n\n## Overlaps\nTouches the same files (different functions/arms; whichever merges second refreshes) with open PRs `#2134`, `#2129`, `#2126`, `#2123`, `#2115`, `#2101`, `#2093`, `#2092`, `#2089`, `#2083`, `#2077`, `#2048`, `#2037`, `#2035`, `#2013`, `#1821`, `#1817`, `#1753`, `#1738`, `#1713`, `#1701`, `#1681`, `#1330`, `#1209`, and `#468`.\n\nChangelog: Carry pure Z-axis WCS rotation through milling toolpath generation and Bake or Control (G68/ROT) posting, and guard 3-2-1 mill face alignment against tilted faces.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nFixes #760\n",
